    <h2>The honest math</h2>
    <p>If your average job value is $500 and a custom site converts even one extra visitor a week into a call, that is $26,000 of additional pipeline a year, before counting the weeks of lost leads if a WordPress site is compromised. If your average job is $5,000, the math is an order of magnitude bigger. <strong>For a service business with 5&ndash;15 pages and a contact form, WordPress is the wrong shape: you are paying for an editorial CMS you do not need, while inheriting a security and performance burden that costs you customers.</strong></p>
